.SS add
Add a Gitea login

.PP
\fB--client-id\fP="": OAuth client ID (for use with --oauth)

.PP
\fB--git-credentials, --helper, -j\fP: Register tea as a git credential helper for this login's URL, so 'git push' and 'git clone' over HTTPS authenticate silently using the stored token

.PP
\fB--help, -h\fP: show help

.PP
\fB--insecure, -i\fP: Disable TLS verification

.PP
\fB--name, -n\fP="": Login name

.PP
\fB--no-version-check, --nv\fP: Do not check version of Gitea instance

.PP
\fB--oauth, -o\fP: Use interactive OAuth2 flow for authentication

.PP
\fB--otp\fP="": OTP token for auth, if necessary

.PP
\fB--password, --pwd\fP="": Password for basic auth (will create token)

.PP
\fB--redirect-url\fP="": OAuth redirect URL (for use with --oauth)

.PP
\fB--scopes\fP="": Token scopes to add when creating a new token, separated by a comma

.PP
\fB--ssh-agent-key, -a\fP="": Use SSH public key or SSH fingerprint to login (needs a running ssh-agent with ssh key loaded)

.PP
\fB--ssh-agent-principal, -c\fP="": Use SSH certificate with specified principal to login (needs a running ssh-agent with certificate loaded)

.PP
\fB--ssh-key, -s\fP="": Path to a SSH key/certificate to use, overrides auto-discovery

.PP
\fB--token, -t\fP="": Access token. Can be obtained from Settings > Applications

.PP
\fB--url, -u\fP="": Server URL (default: "https://gitea.com")

.PP
\fB--user\fP="": User for basic auth (will create token)

